# No environment variables are needed, and none can be added usefully.
#
# The site is a static export with no server, so there is nowhere to keep a
# secret: anything put in here would be compiled into the JavaScript bundle and
# readable by anyone who can open the site.
#
# Nothing the app does needs a credential any more. The log is read from
# data/log.csv at build time, so the browser never authenticates against
# anything, and privacy comes from the repo being private and Cloudflare Access
# sitting in front of the deployed site.
#
# Three keys used to live here and no longer do:
#
#   ANTHROPIC_API_KEY — powered an in-app "Ask Claude" lookup route. That route
#     is gone; Claude Code works out the macros and writes the row instead.
#     Removing it also closed a real hole — the route was unauthenticated, so
#     anyone who found it could spend the credits.
#
#   USDA_API_KEY — powered USDA FoodData Central search. In-app food search is
#     gone entirely along with the add dialog, so neither this nor the
#     key-free Open Food Facts fallback that replaced it is needed.
#
#   GITHUB_TOKEN / gist id — pasted per device for gist sync, which is gone.
#     One file, one writer, no sync.
